{"language_code":"eng","language_probability":0.9761756062507629,"text":"Every company has a Dave. And when Dave leaves, everything he knew walks out the door with him. I've worked at a bunch of private companies, and the hardest thing for all of them wasn't sales or hiring. It was writing down what people know. Someone leaves, and years of context are just gone. And the docs that do exist, stale. Nobody trusts them. [sighs] So people just ask each other over and over. So I tried fixing it for myself first. Obsidian, Notion, all of them. And honestly, the graphs are gorgeous, but making them is so tedious. Every note, you're linking things by hand. [chuckles] It turns into a second job. I always wished it would just do that for me. So I built it. It's called Second Brain. You just throw stuff at it, docs, chats, meeting notes. It reads everything and writes the wiki for you and links it all together automatically. No brackets ever. Ask it anything, and it answers from what your team actually wrote. When something changes, the docs update. They don't go stale. And when someone leaves, what they knew stays. Dave's knowledge, [chuckles] still here. I've been testing it with a few teams, and people are pretty surprised how much it remembers. If your team keeps losing knowledge or you're tired of linking notes by hand, try it. Drop in a folder and watch it build your brain. Links below.","words":[{"text":"Every","start":0.2,"end":0.48,"type":"word","logprob":-0.00001156323378381785},{"text":" ","start":0.48,"end":0.58,"type":"spacing","logprob":-2.9802276912960224e-6},{"text":"company","start":0.58,"end":0.96,"type":"word","logprob":-2.9802276912960224e-6},{"text":" ","start":0.96,"end":1.0,"type":"spacing","logprob":0.0},{"text":"has","start":1.0,"end":1.16,"type":"word","logprob":0.0},{"text":" ","start":1.16,"end":1.22,"type":"spacing","logprob":0.0},{"text":"a","start":1.22,"end":1.3,"type":"word","logprob":0.0},{"text":" ","start":1.3,"end":1.34,"type":"spacing","lo